---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Kit-Bin | Free Browser-Based File Tools"
  description="Kit-Bin is a free collection of PDF, image, audio, video, and data tools that run entirely in your browser. No accounts, no uploads, no installs."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">About Kit-Bin</h1>
    <div class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-4">
      <p>
        Kit-Bin is a collection of free file tools — PDF, image, audio, video, and data — that run
        entirely in your browser. There's no server involved in the actual conversion work; your
        device does it, using WebAssembly and native browser APIs, so the file you select never
        needs to leave it.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's a deliberate choice, not a marketing line. See
        <a href="/guides/how-kit-bin-works" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline"
          >how Kit-Bin actually works</a
        >
        for the technical explanation, including how to verify it yourself using your browser's
        own developer tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is free to use, with no account required, and pays for itself through display
        ads rather than a subscription. If a tool has genuinely helped you, there's also a
        <a href="/contact" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">contact page</a>
        and a way to support the site directly in the footer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Kit-Bin also publishes a small set of
        <a href="/guides/" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">guides</a>
        explaining the file formats and mechanics behind the tools — why iPhone photos won't open
        on Windows, why a PDF is larger than it looks, why a video can sound quiet even at full
        volume — for anyone who wants the actual explanation, not just the conversion.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
